# The behavior of an object type that a package defines. The kernel calls
# it in the transaction of an installation, upgrade or removal, after the
# repository holds the new objects, in an execution that only reads,
# without tenant and user and with a short time limit.
public interface /TRBASE/OBJECT_TYPE_BEHAVIOR

  # Checks the installed and changed objects of the type beyond their
  # structure and references. A message with the severity ERROR, or an
  # exception, rejects the operation; warnings are shown.
  method CHECK(changes: /TRBASE/OBJECT_CHANGE_ARRAY) returns /TRBASE/OBJECT_MESSAGE_ARRAY raises /RT/EXCEPTION

  # Learns that objects of the type were installed, changed or removed,
  # e.g. to drop what it keeps in memory. An exception rejects the
  # operation.
  method CHANGED(changes: /TRBASE/OBJECT_CHANGE_ARRAY) raises /RT/EXCEPTION

end
